  "asked": "# Build: land-round-2 (Current profile) - catch up and land the rest, Molly first Book to **Landin' Lenny**. Register id `land-round-2` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. ## What Brett said (voice, Nov 4 2026) After lenny-land-all, every remaining PR conflicts with main. Brett agreed: one agent catches them up and lands them, **Molly first** (commands must reach the console inside Molly). ## Rules - **ONE PR at a time**: update its branch from current main, fix conflicts (keep every feature from both sides; never drop work), make CI green, merge, next. Post each merge to the builds store. If one fights more than ~20 min, hold it with one plain-English line why and move on. - The VPS is the bottleneck: maxAgents is 1, so you're alone - but still run heavy test/typecheck through agent-slots (max 3 heavy) and **never leave tsc/vite/playwright processes running** after a step. Don't run screenshot passes; UI Review shots are already attached to these PRs. - Tests writing tracked export files (framework/plan/pending.json etc.): `git checkout -- .` before each commit. ## Order 1. **#288** Console commands reach the console inside Molly (RED - fix the failure) - it carries #266 console-wake; if #266 is fully contained, close #266 as superseded, else land #266 right after. 2. #294 Molly banners, #295 Molly nav submenus (they may overlap each other and #288 - merge carefully). 3. #296 Gizmo companion chat. 4. #298 Console lazy loader. 5. #281 Smart menus, #291 Git status board, #293 Terminal tab position. 6. #289 Plugin settings placement (RED), #269 Builds one page (RED) - fix failures. 7. #300 Profile switcher widget. - Do NOT merge the WIP PRs #299 browser-automation, #301 main-area-tabs, #302 app-style-override (paused, unfinished). Close #297 if it's an orphan duplicate of the CI fix. - Redeploy the console + Molly right after #288 lands (confirm a console_show reaches the console inside Molly if you can), then once more at the end for all apps. - Report `_claude/builds/reports/land-round-2.md`: landed / held (why) / closed, cost, time. THREADS. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
